                <pb facs="0641" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg569"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10044/165.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Leishman
                        to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-04-27"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 27, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Leishman requests that instructions be sent to cruisers at Gibraltar to go
                    direct to Mersine and Alexandretta, leaving embassy free, if necessary, to send
                    them to other points.</p>
            </div>
